##   ├ Desktops                                              {{{2
#
# 9 pages on a single Desk (Desk 0). Cells show the Super+<n> binding.
#
#       0   1   2   <- page x
#     +---+---+---+
#   0 | 1 | 2 | 3 |
#     +---+---+---+
#   1 | 4 | 5 | 6 |
#     +---+---+---+
#   2 | 7 | 8 | 9 |
#     +---+---+---+
#   ^ page y
#
EwmhNumberOfDesktops 1 0
DesktopSize 3x3
EdgeScroll 100 100
EdgeResistance -1
EdgeThickness 1
Style * EdgeMoveDelay 250
Style * EdgeMoveResistance 20
Style * EdgeResizeDelay -1

# EwmhBaseStruts [left] [right] [top] [bottom]
# Reserves space along the edge(s) of the Screen that will not
# be covered when maximizing or placing windows.
# The shelf claims one side column; there is no bottom row any more.
##  Shelf width is persisted and adjusted in keyboard steps; this covers the
##  brief interval before the restarted panel re-issues its runtime strut.
PipeRead "$[FVWM_USERDIR]/bin/shelf-panel --print-struts"

