##   ├ Shelf                                                 {{{2
##  The QNX Photon shelf is one program: bin/shelf-panel, over bin/photon.py.
##  It runs the full height of either edge -- there is no taskbar row
##  below it any more, and it carries the window list, tray and clock that
##  row used to hold.  It draws its own frame, headers, launchers, pager,
##  meters and media widget, reads its sections from panel.items and keeps
##  its width, side and collapse state in .panel.state.
##
##  It is not an fvwm module, and that is the point.  FvwmButtons cannot
##  change its layout at runtime -- ChangeButton reaches a button's title,
##  icon and colorset and nothing else -- so collapsing a group meant
##  regenerating the module config and restarting the module, and resizing
##  the shelf meant the same.  A module restart is asynchronous with no
##  "I am mapped" signal to sequence against, so the swap was a timer race
##  that dropped the shelf entirely on about one toggle in four.  And the
##  reference's left edge is two nested bevels, which `Frame N` cannot draw
##  at any N.  All three go away by drawing it ourselves.  PANEL-DESIGN.md
##  is the long version.
##
##  FixedPosition and FixedSize ignore the *user's* attempts to move or
##  resize, not the program's (fvwm3styles.html), so the panel can still
##  move and resize itself as the edge is dragged while nothing else can.
Style "ShelfPanel" !Title, !Handles, BorderWidth 0, HandleWidth 0, \
    Sticky, WindowListSkip, CirculateSkip, NeverFocus, \
    FixedPosition, FixedSize, StaysOnTop
##                                                           }}}2
